            <ArticleTitle>BWH emergency radiology--surgical correlation: traumatic spigelian hernia with right colonic injury.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>709-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s10140-015-1321-x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of a young man who fell off his motorbike 2 days before presentation to the hospital with a complaint of gastrointestinal upset and abdominal pain. Contrast-enhanced CT of the abdomen and pelvis demonstrated a right-sided traumatic spigelian hernia and an ascending colon injury necessitating operative repair of both.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
